), so this is not a volume effect; the global activity peak occurs later at 78322\u201380321, not at the change point (step_10), so no graph-wide surge explains it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_107b45e5\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [59, 83, 325, 610, 617, 642, 743, 826, 881, 991, 1034, 1641],\n  \"window\": [56322, 86322],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"All twelve nodes switch from a shared old partner pool to a disjoint new one within a narrow interval around t=70552: turnover jumps from a ~0.3 baseline to 1.0 and the before/after edge sets have Jaccard 0.0, while the same group shows 0.38-0.54 overlap across comparable adjacent windows elsewhere in the period. Group activity volume is otherwise stable and the graph-wide activity peak falls elsewhere, ruling out volume or popularity artifacts.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 52544, "total_output_tokens": 4625, "total_tokens": 57169, "total_latency_ms": 65764, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}